## Resources

Define your resources in `src/{{ package_name }}/resources/`:

```python
from pragma_sdk import Config, Field, Outputs, Resource


class MyResourceConfig(Config):
    name: Field[str]


class MyResourceOutputs(Outputs):
    url: str


class MyResource(Resource[MyResourceConfig, MyResourceOutputs]):
    async def on_create(self) -> MyResourceOutputs: ...

    async def on_observe(self) -> MyResourceOutputs | None: ...

    async def on_update(self, previous_config: MyResourceConfig | None) -> MyResourceOutputs: ...

    async def on_delete(self) -> None: ...
```

Then register them on the provider in `src/{{ package_name }}/__init__.py`:

```python
from pragma_sdk import Provider

from {{ package_name }}.resources import MyResource

{{ name | replace('-', '_') }} = Provider()

{{ name | replace('-', '_') }}.resource("my_resource")(MyResource)
```

- `on_observe` locates the external object from the resource identity and config alone, returns `None` when it does not exist, and otherwise returns the same outputs the write path returns. Never read `self.outputs`.
- `on_update` receives `previous_config=None` when the object already existed at create.
- A resource with no external object of its own declares `computed = True` and needs no `on_observe`.

## Deployment

Push your provider to Pragmatiks platform:

```bash
pragma provider push
```

The platform handles all runtime infrastructure - you just push your code.

